<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24744" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δια-είδω</span></b>  (A) (i.e.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαϝείδω</span>), fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-είσομαι,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>discern, distinguish,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὔριον ἢν ἀρετὴν διαείσεται</span>
			<i>will test</i> his manhood, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				8.535
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθα μάλιστ᾽ ἀρετὴ διαείδεται</span>”
				<i>is discerned,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					13.277
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SD</u>
				1.1
			</span></i>; simply, <i>appear between,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.579
			</span></i> (tm.).</div>
